# Cloudflare Workers static assets read this file; it is not served.
#
# NO PAGE MAY BE FRAMED, on any path. `frame-ancestors` only works as a header (a browser ignores
# it in a `<meta>` policy), so it is the one directive this file sends.
#
# NO SCRIPT POLICY HERE, and it is not an oversight. A header of `script-src 'self'` stopped the
# inline script that starts every page, measured on 23 September, and the drawn app in the hero
# stopped answering. The script policy is `kit.csp` in `svelte.config.js`, which hashes that script
# into each page. A browser enforces every policy it is sent, so a header `script-src` (or a
# `default-src`, which scripts fall back to) would still block it on top of the meta tag.
# `test/one-origin.test.mjs` fails on one.
#
# THE REST SAYS HOW A PAGE IS REACHED AND WHAT IT MAY ASK FOR, AS EVERY PAGE OF THE APP DOES (`PAGE_HARDENING`,
# `apps/worker/src/route.ts`). Measured on 5 Nov: none of them on brain.dog. HSTS covers the names under this host too
# (includeSubDomains, since 8 Nov), so every one of them must answer on https; it is not preloaded.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), serial=(), hid=(), bluetooth=(), midi=()

# A hashed file never changes under its name, so a browser keeps it for a year and never asks again.
/_app/immutable/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The files here are the link-preview cards, which `scripts/product.mjs` redraws under the same
# names, so a browser keeps one for a day and refreshes it in the background for a week after.
/shots/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

# The fonts are asked for by version (`?v=` in `tokens.css`), so a new face is a new address. A browser keeps
# one for a week and refreshes it in the background for a month after, rather than asking on every visit.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, stale-while-revalidate=2592000

# The Mac app's update feed (`mac/appcast.xml`, Sparkle) is read by every copy once a day: kept five minutes, so a release
# reaches them the same day and the feed is never stale for long.
/mac/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
  Content-Type: application/xml; charset=utf-8
